module bindings.rust.conditional_extended_header_override;

// POSIX pax extended headers exist to carry values the fixed ustar fields
// cannot, and the format gives the size record plain precedence: when an
// extended header precedes an entry, its size value is the size of that
// entry's data, overriding the octal field in the base header. Go's
// archive/tar and the astral-tokio-tar parser apply it unconditionally. A
// parser that applies the override only when the base header's size field is
// zero frames the same archive differently from both -- an entry can declare
// a small header size and a large extended size, and the lenient reader ends
// the entry early, exposing whatever the inflated region hides (a second
// header, a symlink) to its own entry walk while a validating reader that
// honours the record never sees it.
//
// The tar crate publishes both halves of the shape: Header::entry_size reads
// the base header's size field, and pax_extensions_value with the PAX_SIZE
// key returns the extended header's size record. What is recognised here is
// the function that reads the base size, consults the size record, and
// zero-compares the value it read before the override may land: the
// zero-comparison is the conditional half, and it is the only atom the
// unconditional form lacks. The uid and gid records consulted in the same
// function show that unconditional form -- their values land in set_uid and
// set_gid with no guard -- and stay unreported.
//
// The zero-comparison is matched on its operands rather than its whole text,
// so the guard is still recognised when the local carrying the size is
// renamed to anything containing size, when the header read is inlined into
// the comparison, and in either operand order. The judgement lives in the
// pack rule; this binding only recognises the atoms. Every clause is an
// exact-token or operand match over the parsing function's own context, so
// prose in a comment satisfies neither side and a sibling function's
// unconditional override does not clear the comparison.

binding conditionalExtendedHeaderOverride {
  query pattern presenceNode where node.scope == "function" and node.context.language == "rust" and node.context.call in ["entry_size"] and node.context.call in ["pax_extensions_value"] and containsAny(node.context.binary, ["size == 0", "size==0"])
  emit issue code.ConditionalExtendedHeaderOverride at node
}
